From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: artcashin <64659740+artcashin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:20:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): suggestions only on the final answer; retry a
 suggestions-only first step
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On a first-turn tool request, qwen3.6-35b often reasoned "let me search for
the widget" and then emitted only "\n\n<suggestions>…</suggestions>" and
stopped, with no tool call. The suggestions section said "End every response
… Always include the suggestions block, even for short answers" and was the
last instruction in the system prompt; RESPONSE STRUCTURE also forbids prose
before a tool call, so the block was the only text left to write.

Prompt: the section is titled "(final answer only)", says suggestions are
answer text written only after the final tool result and that a tool request
is answered with the tool call alone, and moves from the end of the prompt to
just after the code-execution section ("listed above" -> "listed below").
Format and example are unchanged; the suggest_followups spike variant says
the same.

Loop: when the first model call of a request (no tool result yet this turn)
ends with no tool call and its only text is whitespace plus a suggestions
block, the step is retried once with a fresh text sink and a warning is
logged. A second suggestions-only reply passes through as before.

Measured against qwen3.6-35b, replaying a captured first-turn request with
prompt-suggestions on: before, 2/10 tool calls (8 empty); after, 46/50 tool
calls, 2 empty, 1 text plus suggestions, 1 text only. Trade-off: on a plain
question, replies carrying suggestions fell from 14/15 to 5/15.

Tests: prompt wording and section order; four loop cases (retry once,
second suggestions-only passes through, no retry with answer text, no retry
after a tool ran). bun test tests/ 1014/1014; tsc --noEmit clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
